x/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span style=3D"font-weight=
:700">An age of economic warfare</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25p=
x georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The Jensen Huang affair h=
as come about at a moment when economic warfare is growing in importance. I=
ncreasingly, the world=E2=80=99s most powerful nations are relying on their=
 economic arsenals in addition to their military ones. The long list of wea=
pons includes tariffs, sanctions, export controls and more. And private com=
panies have had to adapt.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georg=
ia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>Government restrictions on inter=
national business dealings have soared in recent years, according to a new =
study. One analyst told me that Washington policy is affecting the bottom l=
ines of companies more now than it has in the previous three decades.</span=
></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 =
15px"><span>And few companies have been as central to the current superpowe=
r rivalry as Nvidia. In 2022, the Biden administration imposed sweeping lim=
itations on China=E2=80=99s access to semiconductors and other computing te=
chnology. One product on the restricted list: the high-end models of Nvidia=
 chips, considered the most advanced in the world. They have given the U.S.=
 a crucial advantage in the fierce race between the U.S. and China to devel=
op the most powerful A.I.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georg=
ia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>China, for its part, has fought =
back, designating companies, including defense giants like Raytheon, Boeing=
 and Lockheed Martin as =E2=80=9Cunreliable entities=E2=80=9D and putting t=
